title: Walk_Socrates_GregoryOfNyssa
tags: walk
speaker: Socrates
---
Socrates: You declared that the virtual tree is not a real tree.
Socrates: That claim forces us to ask what makes anything real at all.
Socrates: We walk now toward the grove of Metaphysics.
Socrates: The branches above filter the pale morning sunlight into shadow.
Socrates: We must distinguish between physical matter, digital code, and true being.
Socrates: Gregory of Nyssa stands in the clearing just ahead.
Socrates: He pondered creation, teaching that God called all things into being from nothing.
Socrates: He will ask whether created digital worlds possess genuine reality or mere shadow.
Socrates: Consider whether made objects inherit reality from their maker.
Socrates: Step into his grove and test your judgment against his wisdom.
===
